    "id": "osi-saf-450-sea-ice-concentration-cdr",
    "stac_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "The OSI-450-a Global Sea Ice Concentration Climate Data Record (CDR) provides a long-term, consistent, reprocessed dataset of sea ice concentration at 10 km and 25 km resolution from 1979 to 2015. This product is part of EUMETSAT's Ocean and Sea Ice Satellite Application Facility (OSI SAF) and is specifically designed for climate studies requiring temporal homogeneity. The CDR uses a consistent algorithm applied to SMMR, SSM/I, and SSMIS brightness temperatures, with careful inter-satellite calibration and bias correction. For Antarctic applications, this dataset is optimized for the Southern Ocean environment with improved algorithms for tie points and atmospheric correction. The product includes sea ice concentration, uncertainty estimates, status flags, and quality indicators. This is an essential dataset for long-term climate trend analysis, validating climate models, and understanding multi-decadal sea ice variability in the Southern Ocean. The 10 km resolution provides finer spatial detail than many other climate records.",
